# Copy this file to .env and fill in the iOS values below. .env is gitignored —
# never commit it. Expo inlines any EXPO_PUBLIC_* variable into the JS bundle at
# build time, no extra package required.
#
# Only iOS-specific Google Sign-In values live here. The existing Firebase config
# and Android/web OAuth client ID stay hardcoded in hooks/useGoogleSignIn.ts (as
# they were before) — moving those to env as well is a separate cleanup, not part
# of adding iOS support, and isn't needed for iOS Google Sign-In to work.

# --- Google Sign-In (iOS only) ---
# Required to make Google Sign-In work on iOS; Android/web ignore these.
# Get them by adding an iOS app to the goye-media Firebase project (if one
# doesn't exist yet) and downloading its GoogleService-Info.plist into the
# project root (same folder as this file) — it's gitignored, so it stays local
# to whoever has Firebase access.
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_IOS_CLIENT_ID  <- the plist's "CLIENT_ID" key
#   EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_IOS_URL_SCHEME <- the plist's "REVERSED_CLIENT_ID" key
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_IOS_CLIENT_ID=
EXPO_PUBLIC_GOOGLE_IOS_URL_SCHEME=
